After you get the book of the dead from Rodney, immediately bless it.
Then you should levelport down to the lowest dungeon level, teleport
directly to the vibrating square, and perform the ritual.  Climb down
the stairs, burn Elbereth, kill any master/arch liches that try to mess
with you, then climb back up, and levelport down. If you have passwall,
you won't even need to hunt for the door to the temple of Moloch.  You
can read from the blessed +BotD to get past most of the undead in the
graveyard, or you can combine a wand of teleportation and jumping (the
spell) to get out of there.

With your advanced stats, the odds of dying through HP loss is very
slight, so you should worry more about the four insta-deaths that can
still mess you up.  Stoning, lava, sickness, and digestion.  Wearing an
amulet of life saving should offer you enough protection, but be sure
not to skip messages.  And if you use up the amulet, put on another one
right away.

If you get caught in a summoning storm, remember that you can drop the
"AoY and levelport to one of your stashes.  There you can fix yourself
up and come back with the means to clear the level.

It might not be the best idea to go through the Planes at level 30.
The risk of getting a level full of Solars between you and the portal
is not one I would recommend.  You can drain yourself down to level 20
or so before entering the Plane of Earth, and drink blessed potions of
full healing to get the levels back on Astral.

There are tricks you can do on Astral, such as permanently killing
Death, and taming Pestilence and Famine.  Alternatively, you can kill
absolutely everything on the level, destroy all objects, and leave the
level completely "spotless".  I don't think I've ever seen that before
- someone ascending completely naked with the Amulet of Yendor as the
ONLY object left in existance on the Astral plane, with no other
monsters left alive. Hint - fill the level with acid blobs, then
genocide them immediately before offering the "AoY.  Use multiple Bags
of Holding to destroy all physical objects, including your entire
inventory (save that for last)

Happy Hacking.



